  bash: "# qsm-langdev's own semgrep rules for bash, run by semgrep-bash beside the\n# registry's. A rule belongs here only when neither the registry nor\n# shellcheck finds it, and each one is proven by rules/bash.fixture:\n# `# ruleid:` above a line it must flag, `# ok:` above one it must not.\n---\nrules:\n  # shellcheck has no check for it (none of its 520 wiki pages names curl,\n  # wget or certificates), and the registry's three bash rules are about\n  # piping or eval-ing the download, not about how it was fetched.\n  - id: qsm.bash.tls-verification-off\n    languages: [bash]\n    severity: WARNING\n    message: >-\n      TLS certificate verification is turned off, so anyone on the network\n      path can answer in the server's place. Fix the trust store or pass the\n      server's CA with --cacert (curl) or --ca-certificate (wget).\n    metadata:\n      category: security\n      cwe:\n        - \"CWE-295: Improper Certificate Validation\"\n    pattern-either:\n      - patterns:\n          - pattern: curl ... $FLAG ...\n          # -k alone or inside a cluster of short flags: -k, -sk, -fsSLk.\n          - metavariable-regex:\n              metavariable: $FLAG\n              regex: ^(--insecure|-[a-zA-Z]*k[a-zA-Z]*)$\n      - pattern: wget ... --no-check-certificate ...\n",
